PRD: docs/prds/v0_3/mesh-morphing-phase-2.md task δ

Real `Projector` trait impl backed by `BRepExtrema_DistShapeShape`. Today the trait at `crates/reify-mesh-morph/src/boundary.rs:161-182` only has a test-only `RecordingProjector` — this task adds the real OCCT-backed implementation.

New file `crates/reify-kernel-occt/src/projector_impl.rs` (or co-located in `handle.rs`; decision at impl time). `OcctProjector` holds `OcctKernel` — by-value, `&OcctKernel`, or `Arc<OcctKernel>` open per PRD §9 Q-9-3 (engine holds `Engine.kernel` for the realization's lifetime which exceeds the morph call).

Implements `reify_mesh_morph::Projector` per PRD §3.4:

```rust
impl reify_mesh_morph::Projector for OcctProjector {
    fn project_onto_face(&self, face: GeometryHandleId, point: [f64; 3])
        -> Result<[f64; 3], ProjectorPayload> { /* BRepExtrema_DistShapeShape(face_topods, vertex_from_point).PointOnShape1() */ }
    fn project_onto_edge(&self, edge: GeometryHandleId, point: [f64; 3])
        -> Result<[f64; 3], ProjectorPayload> { /* same with edge */ }
    fn vertex_position(&self, vertex: GeometryHandleId)
        -> Result<[f64; 3], ProjectorPayload> { /* BRep_Tool::Pnt direct; no closest-point */ }
}
```

`vertex_position` short-circuits the FFI call entirely — kernel already holds the `TopoDS_Vertex` (per task α's `BRepKind::Vertex` registration); coordinates read directly via `BRep_Tool::Pnt`. Matches `boundary.rs:177-181` doc-comment ("vertex projection is a snap to the new vertex's exact coordinates, not a closest-point computation").

FFI is already in the workspace — this is wiring + test work, not new FFI. Existing OCCT-integration tests `crates/reify-kernel-occt/tests/closest_point_on_shape_integration.rs:81-220` and `tests/point_on_shape_integration.rs:119-380` already exercise `BRepExtrema_DistShapeShape` against `TopoDS_Solid`, `TopoDS_Face`, `TopoDS_Edge`, `TopoDS_Vertex`, `TopoDS_Wire`.

User-observable signal: §7.3 boundary test `crates/reify-kernel-occt/tests/projector_impl.rs`:
- Construct `OcctProjector` over a real `OcctKernel` with a box `TopoDS_Solid`.
- For each of `project_onto_face`, `project_onto_edge`, `vertex_position`: query with a fixed off-shape point (none for vertex). Assert returned point matches the BRepExtrema semantics pinned by existing OCCT integration tests.
- Stub-kernel handle returns `Err(ProjectorPayload { message: "kernel returned error: ..." })` with OCCT error text preserved.

Consumer: engine-wire 2947 via `Projector` trait obj passed to `compute_dirichlet_bcs` / elasticity / Laplacian morph paths.

Dependencies: NONE (independent of α/β/γ — Projector impl is testable in isolation against synthetic OCCT handles; FFI already shipped).

Crates touched: reify-kernel-occt.

